### Accessing your Panopto videos via the VLE

<!-- Clear and concise: Click **Submit**, not Click on the **Submit button** -->
<!-- Use **bold** to highight key tasks and features -->

**Step 1:** Log into your [Blackboard Ultra](www.vle.york.ac.uk) account using your university credentials.

**Step 2:** Navigate to the specific module where your video lectures are hosted via the Courses area in the left-hand menu.

![Course menu within Blackboard](Images/courses-in-vle.png)

**Step 3:** On the course page, look for a Panopto link to your video embedded within your module (A). Videos may also be made available under a folder titled "Replay Lecture Capture (Panopto)" wthin the course content, should this folder be available for students to access (B).

![Panopto tool in a VLE module course](Images/panopto-vids-vle.png)

**Step 4:** Click on the Panopto link to access the videos. This will open the Panopto platform embedded in Blackboard Ultra or in a new window.

!!! tip inline end "Making use of Panopto video features"
To make use of Panopto's video features, open the video in Panopto by clicking on the arrow icon in the bottom right-hand corner of the video player. From here you can enable captions and take notes!

![open in panopto arrow within video player](Images/arrow-open-in-panopto.png)

## More Details and Troubleshooting 

**Tip 1:** Ensure you are using a supported browser (Chrome, Firefox). Panopto may not work properly on older browsers or Safari.

**Tip 2:** Clear your browser’s cache or try accessing Panopto from an incognito/private window if you encounter loading issues. Details on how to do this can be found in our [Troubleshooting Guidance](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PV1mw9PiXP6D2UYGrzso8Gnx-aFaugWb4USX_y_h6o0/edit).

**Tip 3:** Check that your internet connection is stable. Video streaming requires a reliable connection.

**Tip 4:** If Panopto videos are not playing, make sure your pop-up blocker is disabled for Blackboard and Panopto websites.

**Tip 5:** Update your browser to the latest version to ensure compatibility with Panopto.

**Tip 6:** If you are still unable to access your videos, contact our team with details of the videos you are trying to access and for which module.

